A||||3||Slammed Fiero||4.0ltr Underhead Cam V8 from GM||||1||
Z||000000||Slammed Fiero||09-27-2001||10:18 AM||||Few friends were overlast night. Both in there 40's work as engineers , and also build some Kiler Datsun / Nissan Z cars for track use.<P>They were approached By GM powertrain for cam phasers for a new motor.<P>4.0ltr  UNDERHEADCAM V8 (4 cam)<P>the cams for this are Inside the block according to Gm powertrain. So you have a 4 cam design with pushrods. Apperently this combo is running around in 4 Saabs in Michigan. Gm powertrain builds the motors and sells them to GM divisions. I thought this engine was a really neat idea , they have been testing them for a few momths now , no word on how they perform , but this engine is being designed to replace the N*<P>This gives you an engine with all the power of 4 cams , but a smaller spread(ie 2.8 is 60 degree , SBC is 90 degree) this engine is a 70 degree motor! , and very compact.<P>Just an FYI ... He also said 4.3's are the cheapest motor GM powertrain builds and sells. They sell them to GM at $1800 for a complete a motor (FI and everything)<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jaei Sun||09-27-2001||10:30 AM||||Hmmm if this design is going to be replacing the N*, I'm betting GM is seeing good perf results in their testing.<P>I see it as more options for us to replace the 2.8 with some power!||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||09-29-2001||01:25 AM||||Hrm, seems overly complex, and how they are going to deal with balance issues in a 70-degree V8 kind of scares me  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (oh, a non-90degree crank, and an external balancer &lt;uugh, I'd thought the world had seen the end of that&gt; could quiet the primary harmonics, but what about the inevetable secondary and tertiary and so on?) Northstar is already an incredibly smooth engine, I'd have suspected it to gain only variable cam timings in later years.<P>Darned of the heads on a Northstar aren't HUGE though, heh.  <P>Still, it's not that big a motor, and direct-acting DOHC just seems the purest form of moving valves (ok, excepting desmo type valve actuation, or solonoids...)<P>Sounds like a cool crowd, engineers are always fun to streatch your brain!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>Few friends were overlast night. Both in there 40's work as engineers , and also build some Kiler Datsun / Nissan Z cars for track use.<P>They were approached By GM powertrain for cam phasers for a new motor.<P>4.0ltr  UNDERHEADCAM V8 (4 cam)<P>the cams for this are Inside the block according to Gm powertrain. So you have a 4 cam design with pushrods. Apperently this combo is running around in 4 Saabs in Michigan. Gm powertrain builds the motors and sells them to GM divisions. I thought this engine was a really neat idea , they have been testing them for a few momths now , no word on how they perform , but this engine is being designed to replace the N*<P>This gives you an engine with all the power of 4 cams , but a smaller spread(ie 2.8 is 60 degree , SBC is 90 degree) this engine is a 70 degree motor! , and very compact.<P>Just an FYI ... He also said 4.3's are the cheapest motor GM powertrain builds and sells. They sell them to GM at $1800 for a complete a motor (FI and everything)<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||Leper||09-29-2001||01:42 AM||||I heard that the 4.0 was going to be used in cars that currently have engine bays that can only fit 4 and 6cyls. Say a Malibu (sunfire even?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">?) something like that. I didn't think it's going to be a N* replacement. Northstar tooling is capable of making a 5.4L engine too or so I heard. So maybe the Northstar is moving up replace the pushrod v8.<P>Look for even more funky 4's and 6's to arrive in the future that would be great for Fiero engine swaps.||||reg||1
